                    },
                    "message": "Where did this come from?  When in EM mode, there's no SamplePeriod, it's all match expression based, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/pid.json",
                    "line": 104,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I did not dive into phosphor-pid-control, but they do mention this property in their configuration guides.\n\nhttps://github.com/search?q=org%3Aopenbmc%20samplePeriod&type=code\n\nIt is definitely configured somewhere, else i would not have added this property.\n\nDo you think it makes sense to remove the property ```samplePeriod``` from the configurations instead of adding it to the schema? It sounds like you know more about the pid-control."
                }
